                <pb facs="0519" n="399" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg399"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">814.00/1044: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Whitehouse</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-01-05T17:00:00-07:00">January 5, 1931—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:55 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>7. The decree calling elections for President to take place on February 6th, 7th
                    and 8th was issued on January 3rd.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Whitehouse</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
